/* PowerPod Platform — digitised CAD geometry.
 *
 * Every number below was read out of the source models, not drawn by hand:
 *
 *   D              PP_ASM_V1.5_REV3(FLEX).STEP, in mm, y-up.
 *                  three.x = CAD X (length) · three.y = CAD Z (height)
 *                  three.z = CAD Y (depth)
 *   HANDLE_CURVES  HLR silhouette of PP_HND_WTH_CVR V1.5 R2.
 *   BSBMS          the BMS board: outline frame plus component islands, and
 *                  L[], the island offsets for each alternate layout.
 *   XCONN          PP_XCONN_ENC_F V1.5, all 80 drilled features as
 *                  [x, z, radius, depth0, depth1].
 *   PULSE          Pulse V2.0 telematics board out of KiCad: c[] = 338
 *                  components as [x0,y0,x1,y1,height], h[] = 12 holes.
 *   IOT            power-board parts, BMS components and the 60 nickel
 *                  interconnect strips, each [x,y,z,sx,sy,sz].
 *   HX             PP_ASM_V1.obj, the handle assembly's own mesh. The five
 *                  bodies that make it up (two mounting blocks, the grip bar
 *                  and two screws) all proved exactly convex — every one of
 *                  their 11,472 vertices lies on its own convex hull to
 *                  0.0000mm — so their hulls ARE the geometry. v[] = vertices
 *                  in the OBJ's own frame, expressed along the top face's
 *                  diagonal (u -77.67..77.67 across it, w across the width,
 *                  h up from the cap face); e[] = the 503 true feature edges,
 *                  every edge where the surface turns by more than 18
 *                  degrees; t[] = the hull triangles that occlude them;
 *                  g[] = the vertex range of each body.
 *   PODART         PP_DOCK_PACK_ASM_EMPT.STEP as an actual hidden-line view,
 *                  391.31 x 132.20 mm quantised to 0.003mm: out (outlines),
 *                  sharp (creases), rg1 (smooth/tangent boundaries) each
 *                  base64-packed as uint16 deltas, plus sil, the closed
 *                  silhouette the occluder is filled from.
 *
 * Kept apart from scripts/cinema.js purely so that file stays editable: one
 * line here is 38KB.
 */

